  TOURNAMENT ANALYSIS ON CUBE-ROOT PROOF LENSES
    leaders={'actual_residual': (0, 5, 10, 11, 12, 13, 14, 15, 16, 17), 'pair_tax_shadow': (0, 4, 6, 8, 10, 12, 14, 15, 16, 17), 'eisenstein_imbalance': (0, 4, 6, 8, 10, 12, 14, 15, 16, 17), 'direct_p0': (0, 9, 10, 11, 12, 13, 14, 15, 16, 17)}
    score_hist={0: 1, 1: 1, 2: 1, 3: 1}
    Hamiltonian_path=direct_p0 > eisenstein_imbalance > pair_tax_shadow > actual_residual
    challenged assumption: cube-root imbalance is not automatically direct risk.

SYNTHESIS
  A+B+C-D-E-F+G is exact, but it is the pair-tax shadow H(1)-2*R2, not the cap residual.
  The cube-root modes split cyclic imbalance among singles and pairs without numeric approximation.
  The useful proof lens is a three-coordinate packet: actual residual, pair-tax shadow,
  and Eisenstein imbalance.  These can rank different rows, so none should be collapsed early.
